=========================================================================
4. CHECKER-FORCED DEVIATION (noted per R6 / WO §Verify)
=========================================================================
  a#59 / b#39 ask for the Italian ordinal in “dal 1 gennaio 2024”, “dal 1 luglio 2026”, etc.
  Writing “1°” (or “1º”, or “primo”) breaks `checkNumbers` for `it`: the date matcher stops
  recognising the D-month-YYYY pattern and the year is then read as two tokens.

      $ node -e "extractNormalizedNumbers('dal 1 gennaio 2024.','it')"   -> [1, 1, 2024]   OK
      $ node -e "extractNormalizedNumbers('dal 1° gennaio 2024.','it')"  -> [1, 20, 1, 24] FAIL
      $ node -e "extractNormalizedNumbers('dal primo gennaio 2024.','it')" -> [1, 20, 24]  FAIL

  With “1°” the run was `summary FAIL 14/18` (001, 004, 011, 015: “missing 2024/2025/2026,
  extra 20/24/25/26”). Per R6 the previous form was kept for those 8 dates and the deviation is
  recorded here. Everything else in a#44 (ISO dates → “29 maggio 2026”, “a decorrere dal 1 luglio
  2026”) was applied and passes.

