7. WHERE I DISAGREED WITH THE REVIEWERS (not applied as written)
=========================================================================
  1. a#5 — “per un investitore italiano vale di regola la ritenuta interna del 21 %”. Wrong twice:
     it asserts a rule about the reader’s country (forbidden by ACCEPTED and by R2d) and it is not
     in the English source. Applied the neutral R2b note instead.
  2. a#22 / a#56 — same problem (“non un trasferimento dall’Italia”, “per esempio Italia e Taiwan”).
     Naming Italy also fails the checker’s `nationality` gate. Neutralized.
  3. a#13 — “cerchia dei suoi azionisti”. For 股東 the natural Italian company-law term is
     “compagine azionaria”; “cerchia” was kept only for eredi / convenuti.
  4. a#34 — “Leggi di più”. Used the supervisor’s “Continua a leggere” (sup#9) instead; both are
     tu-imperatives, the supervisor’s decision governs.
  5. a#37 — “Di seguito, risposte a livello di indicazioni generali.” is a fragment; used the
     supervisor’s full clause (sup#8).
  6. b#5 — “lettera con avviso di ricevimento e contenuto certificato”. 存證信函 is not a
     return-receipt letter; the content is what the post office certifies. Used “lettera
     raccomandata con certificazione del contenuto”.
  7. a-verdict praise for 007’s “rapporti personali (會面交往)” — I still changed it. R8 requires one
     term per locale and the supervisor fixed the guidance pack to “il diritto di visita”; leaving
     two different renderings of 會面交往 on the same site would be worse than the small loss.
  8. a#14’s alternative (“drop the fact”) — not taken; ACCEPTED keeps the TWD 1,57 mln first-instance
     judgment and only the presentation was fixed.
  9. b#14 — the Invest Taiwan `lang=jpn` link is genuinely still wrong, but changing links is
     outside the hard rules and ACCEPTED marks the row as already fixed. Left untouched and
     escalated in §3.
